    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1115">

                <pb facs="1405" n="1395" sameAs="frus:frus1947v07/pg1395"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.5293/6–1047: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Shanghai</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Davis</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-06-10T15:00:00+09:00">June 10, 1947—3
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received June 10—3:15 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1400. Shanghai Bureau of Land Administration has not yet replied to Consulate
                    General’s request for general extension of time limit for registration on behalf
                    unknown American landowners (mytel 800, May 8, repeated Department as 1123, May
                    8, 7 p.m. and my despatch to Department No. 1205, May 13<anchor n="22"
                        xml:id="d1115-f1"/>). Land Bureau apparently has adopted practice of
                    granting extension of 1 month in cases where Consulate General has notified it
                    of names of individuals who were unable comply with original time limit. In
                    reply to such notifications Land Bureau sends mimeographed letter pertinent part
                    of which reads “since the said owner has factual difficulty permission is hereby
                    granted to reserve the time limit for application for 1 month from the <pb
                        facs="1406" n="1396" xml:id="pg1396"/> date of receipt of this letter.” In
                    most cases this gives owners until mid-July to register. Consulate General will,
                    if necessary, request further extensions for those who are unable to comply
                    within this extended period of 1 month.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Davis</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
